  {
   "id": 16,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -700,
    0
   ],
   "size": [
    660,
    740
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 15,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Element Forge\n\n**Run** once the clip and the effect are set. The comp shows on **EF Export**, the track check on **EF Track**, the element on\n**EF Element**. Everything goes to `output/element-forge/<run>/` (comp MP4, EXR passes, the settings).\n\n1. **Load Video**: your clip (a file in ComfyUI's input folder).\n2. **EF Shot**: depth model and day for night. Pictures from other nodes go to *images*, a single picture to *picture*.\n3. **EF Track**: click into the first frame for point A, Shift+click for point B. A word for what you clicked helps the\n   tracker. *Follows*: point, the whole object, the scene, or the screen.\n4. **EF Element**: the effect and its style. Leave the words empty for the tested look. The template starts on\n   *quality preview* (half the size, about 3 instead of 7 minutes) for AI styles on black; set *full* for the final and\n   for styles rendered into the clip.\n5. **EF Place**: size, side, depth and blend in the clip.\n6. **EF Light & Glow**: the light the effect casts and its glow. Change only these and Run again: the effect is not made again.\n7. **EF Export**: which passes are written.\n\n**Options** (bypassed, select and press Ctrl+B to use one): EF Particles, EF Guide (with its drawing), EF Dissolve,\nEF LTX Options, your own object mask, an element from the library. Without them the style's tested values hold.\nMore fields: *Show advanced inputs* in a node's menu.\n\n**EF Models**: which LTX files this computer uses.\nTo use the results in other nodes, add **EF Unpack** from Element Forge/Tools: it gives plate, depth, normals, object\nmask, element, light, glow and comp."
   ]
  }
 ],
